// Rule: [T1204.002] Waterplum - VS Code Trusted Project Child Process
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1204.002
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Validates whether processes launched by Visual Studio Code tasks are represented with a direct Code.exe parent and retain
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for vs code trusted project child process using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// WaterPlum / Contagious Interview — VS Code child-process telemetry validation
// Classification: Validation query — Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required table: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: validate whether task-triggered child processes from VS Code are
// represented with Code.exe as their direct initiating process and retain
// sufficient command-line context for later detection engineering.
// Important: results are not malicious by themselves. Normal builds, tests,
// terminals, extensions, package managers, and developer automation overlap.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "Code.exe"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessUniqueId, ProcessUniqueId, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
